<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-CANADA BEAT SWEDEN 2-1 TO WIN WORLD TITLE.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-CANADA BEAT SWEDEN 2-1 TO WIN WORLD TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the third game in the</p>
<p>best-of-three ice hockey world championship pool A final on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>Canada 2 Sweden 1 (1-0 1-0 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Canada - Dean Evason (18:39), Owen Nolan (21:56)</p>
<p>Sweden - Michael Nylander (58:43)</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 14 minutes, Sweden 12 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,181.</p>
<p>Canada win gold medal, two games to one.</p>
</text>
